      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> A practice, not a prescription</p>
      <div class="intro-row"><h2>Small steps can<br>shift the whole day.</h2><p>Mind Ease is a self-guided wellness companion for the everyday ups and downs. Notice what you’re feeling, make space for a new perspective, and find a next step that feels manageable.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-band">
      <div class="wrap feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-item"><span class="feature-number">01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Notice</p><h3>Check in with yourself</h3><p>Track your mood and the little things around it, like sleep, screen time, or a moment that mattered.</p><a href="/register" class="text-link">Mood check-ins <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
        <article class="feature-item"><span class="feature-number">02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Reframe</p><h3>Untangle a thought</h3><p>A guided CBT diary helps you look at the evidence and find a kinder, more balanced perspective.</p><a href="/register" class="text-link">Thought diary <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
        <article class="feature-item"><span class="feature-number">03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Restore</p><h3>Come back to now</h3><p>Try a grounding exercise, a mindful pause, or a supportive conversation with USHA.</p><a href="/register" class="text-link">Explore self-care <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-band wrap"><p class="eyebrow">A gentle reminder</p><div class="closing-row"><h2>Support for the moment.<br>Space for what’s next.</h2><a class="button button-dark" href="/register">Make a little space <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="disclaimer">Mind Ease is a self-help tool, not a substitute for professional mental health care. If you’re in immediate danger, contact your local emergency services.</p></section>
